#. type: Plain text
#: build/C/man7/landlock.7:12
msgid "Landlock - unprivileged access-control"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: build/C/man7/landlock.7:22
msgid ""
"Landlock is an access-control system that enables any processes to securely "
"restrict themselves and their future children.  Because Landlock is a "
"stackable Linux Security Module (LSM), it makes it possible to create safe "
"security sandboxes as new security layers in addition to the existing "
"system-wide access-controls.  This kind of sandbox is expected to help "
"mitigate the security impact of bugs, and unexpected or malicious behaviors "
"in applications."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: build/C/man7/landlock.7:28
msgid ""
"A Landlock security policy is a set of access rights (e.g., open a file in "
"read-only, make a directory, etc.)  tied to a file hierarchy.  Such policy "
"can be configured and enforced by processes for themselves using three "
"system calls:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: build/C/man7/landlock.7:31
msgid "B<landlock_create_ruleset>(2)  creates a new ruleset;"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: build/C/man7/landlock.7:34
msgid "B<landlock_add_rule>(2)  adds a new rule to a ruleset;"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: build/C/man7/landlock.7:37
msgid "B<landlock_restrict_self>(2)  enforces a ruleset on the calling thread."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: build/C/man7/landlock.7:42
msgid ""
"To be able to use these system calls, the running kernel must support "
"Landlock and it must be enabled at boot time."
msgstr ""

#. type: SS
#: build/C/man7/landlock.7:42
#, no-wrap
msgid "Landlock rules"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: build/C/man7/landlock.7:48
msgid ""
"A Landlock rule describes an action on an object which the process intends "
"to perform.  A set of rules is aggregated in a ruleset, which can then "
"restrict the thread enforcing it, and its future children."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: build/C/man7/landlock.7:50
msgid "The two existing types of rules are:"
msgstr ""

#. type: TP
#: build/C/man7/landlock.7:50
#, no-wrap
msgid "B<Filesystem rules>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: build/C/man7/landlock.7:55
msgid ""
"For these rules, the object is a file hierarchy, and the related filesystem "
"actions are defined with I<filesystem access rights>."
msgstr ""

#. type: TP
#: build/C/man7/landlock.7:55
#, no-wrap
msgid "B<Network rules> (since ABI v4)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: build/C/man7/landlock.7:61
msgid ""
"For these rules, the object is a TCP port, and the related actions are "
"defined with I<network access rights>."
msgstr ""

#. type: SS
#: build/C/man7/landlock.7:61
#, no-wrap
msgid "Filesystem actions"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: build/C/man7/landlock.7:71
msgid ""
"These flags enable to restrict a sandboxed process to a set of actions on "
"files and directories.  Files or directories opened before the sandboxing "
"are not subject to these restrictions.  See B<landlock_add_rule>(2)  and "
"B<landlock_create_ruleset>(2)  for more context."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: build/C/man7/landlock.7:73
msgid "The following access rights apply only to files:"
msgstr ""

#. type: TP
#: build/C/man7/landlock.7:73
#, no-wrap
